    turnFlow: 'FOUR-CARD GOLF:\n1. Players arrange 4 cards face down in square; view 2 nearest cards once\n2. Player left of dealer starts\n3. On your turn, either: - Draw from stock, optionally replace a layout card (discard replaced card) - Take top discard, must use to replace layout card - Knock (ends play after others take one more turn)\n4. Cannot look at layout cards before deciding which to replace\n5. If you look at a face-down card, you must replace it SIX-CARD GOLF:\n1. 6 cards arranged 2x3, usually all face down initially\n2. Draw and replace as in 4-card\n3. Replacement cards placed face up\n4. Play ends when one player has all cards face up',
